tory traversal. The `ArtifactStore` service handles filesystem I/O, while access control is enforced at the MCP tool level.\n\n3. **Current Limitation**: **Artifact propagation from task launch to spawned workers is not yet implemented.** There is no mechanism for:\n   - Declaring which artifacts a worker produces\n   - Inheriting artifacts from parent workers\n   - Validating artifact availability before spawning\n   - Discovering available artifacts efficiently\n\n4. **Proposed Solution**: 9 architectural changes documented, including:\n   - Extend `SpawnRequest` with `required_artifacts`, `inherited_artifacts`, and `artifact_inheritance_chain` fields\n   - Update prompt construction to include artifact metadata\n   - Add `producedArtifacts` support to `worker_turn` RPC\n   - Implement planner integration for automatic artifact inheritance\n   - Add `collect_artifacts` MCP tool for worker-side discovery\n\nThe full diagnosis with implementation guidance, acceptance criteria, and evidence citations has been written to the artifact: **task-launch-architecture-diagnosis.md**\n\nThe planner has been notified and will proceed with the next steps.","ttft_ms":5153,"ttft_stream_ms":2258,"time_to_request_ms":145,"type":"result","duration_ms":253641,"uuid":"6954cab4-3e29-46c9-84db-6a55dd521309"}
